---
source: https://cheflindseyfarr.com/old-fashioned-sour-cream-cake-donuts
serves: 13
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
total time: 3 hours
tags:
  - breakfast
  - doughnuts
  - lindsey-farr
---

In a #large bowl{}, #whisk{} together @pastry flour{4.75%cups}, @baking powder{1%Tbsp}, and @kosher salt{1%Tbsp} to distribute. Set aside.

Line a #large mixing bowl{} with #plastic wrap{} and spray the surface with #nonstick cooking spray{}. Set aside.

In the bowl of a #stand mixer{} fitted with the paddle attachment, beat together @granulated sugar{1.25%cups} and @unsalted butter{2.5%Tbsp} on high speed until the butter is completely incorporated.

Add @egg yolks{5} and continue to beat on high until the mixture lightens and increases in volume, about ~{2%minutes}. Stop and scrape down the bowl as needed so it is evenly incorporated.

With the stand mixer on low, gradually add the dry ingredients a large spoonful at a time alternating with spoonfuls of @sour cream{1.5%cups}. Add each spoonful when only a few large streaks of flour remain. Stop the mixer to scrape in the last bit of sour cream, mixing only until the dry ingredients are fully incorporated so the dough remains tender.

Transfer dough to the plastic wrap-lined bowl. Spray the top of the dough with nonstick cooking spray and fold the plastic edges over to cover. Refrigerate for ~{60%minutes} (or up to 2 days).

Line a #half-sheet baking pan{} with #parchment paper{} and spray with nonstick cooking spray. Set aside.

Lightly dust a work surface with flour. Turn the dough out onto the floured work surface, floured side down, and lightly dust the top with more flour.

Working quickly to keep dough cool, roll out dough to 1/2-inch thick.

Brush off excess flour. Use #3-inch ring cutter{} and #1.25-inch ring cutter{} dipped in flour to cut the donuts and holes. Place donuts and holes on the prepared sheet pan.

Cover loosely with #plastic wrap{}, ensuring it does not touch the donuts, and chill in the refrigerator for at least ~{30%minutes} (or up to overnight).

In a #medium bowl{}, #whisk{} together @whole milk{1/3%cup}, @powdered sugar{3.25%cups}, and @kosher salt{1%tsp} to make the glaze. Cover the surface directly with plastic wrap to prevent a skin from forming.

Pour @vegetable oil{96%oz} into a #Dutch oven{} or deep fryer to a depth of at least 2 inches. Attach a #deep-fry thermometer{} and heat oil to 350°F to 360°F.

Gently drop 3-5 donuts into the hot oil. Once they rise to the surface, fry for ~{30%seconds}, flip with a #slotted spoon{}, and fry for ~{80%seconds} until golden brown. Flip again and fry for another ~{80%seconds} until evenly golden brown. Transfer to a #wire rack{} set over a sheet pan. Fry donut holes for ~{30%seconds}, flip, fry ~{60%seconds}, flip, and fry for 40 to ~{60%seconds} until puffed and golden brown all over.

While still hot, dip each donut into the glaze and return to the wire rack to set.
